{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/js/npm_script.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-31T01:15:38.170596Z","id":"afc48d8aaf9bcb98dcb4b6b56bc214c6d44cff59c9efd10b1ad6b7fca85a4d09","body":{"detail":"Measured on macOS (APFS, so each file is a clone, still one lstat, mkdir, clone and chmod per file). A filtered //plugins/pi:test run (-t 'tier 5') launched directly: vitest's RUN line at 14-16 s, its summary 2 s later. Twelve such runs at once: RUN at about 16-19 s each, vitest done 3.5 s later. In bazelisk test //plugins/pi:test --runs_per_test=12 --test_arg=test/clax.test.ts, each run's test.xml time was about 267 s against vitest's Duration of about 29 s. Under 18 runs at once it reached about 500 s per run. The removal at exit, which cost as much again, is gone for tests since dd81962f5 (a copy in TEST_TMPDIR is left for Bazel). The copy has two reasons (this file's header): Vite's native resolver follows Bazel's links while JavaScript does not, so one file gets two paths; and a run sees only declared files. Options: (a) one shared, content-keyed, read-only copy of each project's node_modules per output base, made once and linked into each run's copy (largest win; needs a key over the declared package files and a cleanup in scripts/bazel-gc.sh); (b) link node_modules (or its .aspect_rules_js store) to the real tree instead of copying it: the two-path risk the header names, to be tried per consumer (vitest, vite, tsc, the real Pi of crates/clax-testkit) before relying on it; (c) leave it, accepting that the Pi and web lanes cost tens of seconds of copying per run.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":121},"end":{"line":153},"content_hash":"196cc4ac2ec9cc8ae42fb245677fa0064c3caac6fb6ba3879f4ddfda3d6b7418"},"summary":"Every npm_script_test run copies the whole project, node_modules included (about 83,000 files for plugins/pi), before its script starts: the copy, not the tests, is most of a Pi test's time","tags":["perf","tests","bazel","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/js/npm_script.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T03:20:35.702994Z","id":"0af95b00cf7cd1b1526465e8d7da43cd03bc1049470a501b6540ceed0d4b9606","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:690ff455d","summary":"Fixed by option (b): the copy (now bazel/js/project-copy.mjs) links each package in rules_js's store to its real place instead of copying it, and copies only the project's own files. //bazel/js:project_copy_test checks that no package file is copied. scripts/bazel-web.test.sh still passes all four steps (a deleted module fails, a deleted test no longer runs, a package removed from the lockfile is not found). Tried per consumer: //plugins/pi:test, //plugins/pi:typecheck, //web:lint, :typecheck, :unit (after web/vitest.config.ts allows the store under server.fs.allow), :bundle_size, :sdk_package, :e2e_gesture, :e2e_chrome_overlay, :e2e_queues, :e2e_rest, //web/reel:camera_test and :agent_determinism all pass. Same loaded machine (load average 28-48), old runner against new: //plugins/pi:test 856 s against 130 s, //plugins/pi:typecheck a timeout against 41 s.","supersedes":"afc48d8aaf9bcb98dcb4b6b56bc214c6d44cff59c9efd10b1ad6b7fca85a4d09","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:968df500-9d58-4966-a894-2996308008b5"]}}
